    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-47455",
      "knowledge_point_id": "0e2a8cf2-64db-5b2f-b0f7-0c727cf492a9",
      "knowledge_point": "Describing Properties of the Secant Function",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x?$\n\nI. The period of the function is $\\pi .$\n\nII. The function is increasing in the interval $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].$\n\nIII. The function has no zeros.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934039/assets/779d7a31646a229492a8165c8212a5c83ad7d37d843c1c1b3b36766a74bc5124.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The period of the function is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $y=sec⁡x$ is decreasing on $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has no zeros.",
