    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-103685",
      "knowledge_point_id": "0e2a8cf2-64db-5b2f-b0f7-0c727cf492a9",
      "knowledge_point": "Describing Properties of the Secant Function",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=sec⁡x?$\n\n- The range of the function is $y=(-\\infty ,-1]$\n- $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ is an output of the function\n- $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is not a zero of the function",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934039/assets/d0f3e760be991c936baf5e9825cd582f086a73a8330032d24fd35fd5594b4864.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Therefore, $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ is not an output of the function.\n\n- Statement III is true since the function has no zeros.",
